    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec (and the two acceptance tests on `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`) required: an owner's `registrationDate` defaults to the server's current date when omitted, is preserved when supplied, and is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The generator maps `format: date` \u2192 `LocalDate`, so it appears on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response), and Jackson serializes it as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` (model)** \u2014 added a `registration_date` column mapped to a `LocalDate registrationDate` field with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the endpoint step that builds the entity from the body. After mapping, if `registrationDate` is null it defaults to `LocalDate.now()`; a supplied value passes through untouched.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run against hsqldb; the others kept consistent).\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest`: `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` both pass.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nNo new endpoint pipeline was needed \u2014 the requirement was a field/default within the existing `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline, so the change lives in the `build` step per the project's function-injection conventions rather than a Spring controller.",
